// QC: Better Immersion to Baldur's Gate - BG0100
// Translation strings extracted from bg0100_baldurs_gate.d; original English preserved.

@1 = ~Rogh not won't trouble. Rogh think you very small but scary.~
@2 = ~Rogh is such a nice human... ehm, humanoid. He is an obliging neighbour. At least he isn't like a drow. These dark scum are polluting this glorious city with their presence.~
@3 = ~Phi.~
@4 = ~Dos tris, jalil. Feeling is mutual.~
@5 = ~I used to be an adventurer like you, then I took an arrow to the knee.~
@6 = ~Watch out for Maulers of Undermountain.~
@7 = ~Who?~
@8 = ~They group of adventurers led by Gretek. Once a local cutpurse who got tired of roistering life within city walls and gathered up a party made of ex members of Thieves Guild. Everyone down this street knows them. In fact, one of these houses belonged to Gretek himself. Mere weeks ago, the current owner of the house was murdered. You understand why suspicioun automatically rashes toward Gretek, don't you? His comrades are each thugs and ruffians. Arlin, for example is an elven mage who allegedly was banished from Evermeet for secret cooperation with Drow community - biggest foes to the elves.~
@9 = ~Keep my words in mind. Folk around here dread Maulers of Undermountain and to be frank, I do too.~
@10 = ~Yes, precisely. If Gretek's band is made out of such uncivilised, raw material bandits wannabes, your mind doesn't require much effort to actualise the gravity of the situation.~
@11 = ~Keep my words in mind. Folk around here dread Maulers of Undermountain and to be frank, I do too.~
@12 = ~Elves end up banished from our lands only for committing severe crimes against elven society, breaking sacred laws, or practicing prohibited forms of magic. Actively working to undermine the isolationist policies, stirring up dangerous political dissent, or violating the strict edicts of the ruling nobility is punishable harsly. Elves uphold zero-tolerance policy regarding collusions with the Drow.~
@13 = ~It's mind boggling how patronising some people are against my kin. Halfling are genetically more likely to inherit traits associated with high levels of compassion. We are supernaturally blessed with The Halfling Luck, and do not harbor the same desperate existential anxieties, jealousy, or resource-scarcity panic that drives other mortal races toward greed and tyranny. Exceptions do exist, no question about that, but why can't we all just be nice to one another.~
@14 = ~If you have business with Entar Silvershield, come in. If you do not, I ask you kindly to vacate this property. Entar has no time to spare for commoners, no offence intended.~
@15 = ~Iron Throne is fishy. First, my kin down south caused all that trouble in the mines, then this Sarevok made his grand appearance. I don't like the guy one bit.~
@16 = ~Watch out for the flowers. Took me a while to plant them.~
